# Information about `TIFFSwabArrayOfDouble`

## Function Signature

```c

extern void TIFFSwabArrayOfDouble(double* dp, tmsize_t n);
```

## Source Code

```c
void TIFFSwabArrayOfDouble(double *dp, tmsize_t n) {
  register unsigned char *cp;
  register unsigned char t;
  assert(sizeof(double) == 8);
  /* XXX unroll loop some */
  while (n-- > 0) {
    cp = (unsigned char *)dp;
    t = cp[7];
    cp[7] = cp[0];
    cp[0] = t;
    t = cp[6];
    cp[6] = cp[1];
    cp[1] = t;
    t = cp[5];
    cp[5] = cp[2];
    cp[2] = t;
    t = cp[4];
    cp[4] = cp[3];
    cp[3] = t;
    dp++;
  }
}
```

2026-08-28 19:57:46
Response for query 8 after 0.87s:
Swaps byte order of each `double` in-place for `n` elements. Use it on arrays when TIFF data endianness differs from host. It assumes `sizeof(double)==8`; `n==0` does nothing.
