# Information about `TIFFSwabFloat`

## Function Signature

```c

extern void TIFFSwabFloat(float*);
```

## Source Code

```c
void TIFFSwabFloat(float* fp) {
  register unsigned char* cp = (unsigned char*)fp;
  unsigned char t;
  assert(sizeof(float) == 4);
  t = cp[3];
  cp[3] = cp[0];
  cp[0] = t;
  t = cp[2];
  cp[2] = cp[1];
  cp[1] = t;
}
```

2026-08-28 19:58:51
Response for query 78 after 0.87s:
`TIFFSwabFloat` byte-swaps a 4-byte `float` in place. Use it on a valid `float*` when converting between endianness. It asserts `sizeof(float)==4`; otherwise behavior is not supported.
