# Information about `LogLuv24fromXYZ`

## Function Signature

```c

extern uint32_t LogLuv24fromXYZ(float*, int);
```

## Source Code

```c
uint32_t
LogLuv24fromXYZ(float XYZ[3], int em) {
  int Le, Ce;
  double u, v, s;
  /* encode luminance */
  Le = LogL10fromY(XYZ[1], em);
  /* encode color */
  s = XYZ[0] + 15. * XYZ[1] + 3. * XYZ[2];
  if (!Le || s <= 0.) {
    u = U_NEU;
    v = V_NEU;
  } else {
    u = 4. * XYZ[0] / s;
    v = 9. * XYZ[1] / s;
  }
  Ce = uv_encode(u, v, em);
  if (Ce < 0) /* never happens */
    Ce = uv_encode(U_NEU, V_NEU, SGILOGENCODE_NODITHER);
  /* combine encodings */
  return (Le << 14 | Ce);
}
```

2026-08-28 20:00:52
Response for query 225 after 0.95s:
Encodes XYZ to a 24-bit LogLuv pixel: 10-bit log luminance + 14-bit chroma. Use with `XYZ[3]` and encoding mode `em`. If Y is zero/invalid or `s<=0`, it falls back to neutral u,v. `Ce<0` is handled by neutral fallback.
