# Information about `TIFFSwabDouble`

## Function Signature

```c

extern void TIFFSwabDouble(double*);
```

## Source Code

```c
void TIFFSwabDouble(double* dp) {
  register unsigned char* cp = (unsigned char*)dp;
  unsigned char t;
  assert(sizeof(double) == 8);
  t = cp[7];
  cp[7] = cp[0];
  cp[0] = t;
  t = cp[6];
  cp[6] = cp[1];
  cp[1] = t;
  t = cp[5];
  cp[5] = cp[2];
  cp[2] = t;
  t = cp[4];
  cp[4] = cp[3];
  cp[3] = t;
}
```

2026-08-28 20:01:39
Response for query 281 after 1.08s:
`TIFFSwabDouble` byte-swaps a `double` in place for endian conversion. Pass a valid `double*`; it reverses the 8 bytes directly. It assumes `sizeof(double)==8` (asserts). Use it only when converting between little- and big-endian data.
