# Information about `TIFFWriteRawTile`

## Function Signature

```c

extern tmsize_t TIFFWriteRawTile(TIFF* tif, uint32_t tile, void* data, tmsize_t cc);
```

## Source Code

```c
tmsize_t
TIFFWriteRawTile(TIFF* tif, uint32_t tile, void* data, tmsize_t cc) {
  static const char module[] = "TIFFWriteRawTile";

  if (!WRITECHECKTILES(tif, module))
    return ((tmsize_t)(-1));
  if (tile >= tif->tif_dir.td_nstrips) {
    TIFFErrorExt(tif->tif_clientdata, module, "Tile %lu out of range, max %lu",
                 (unsigned long)tile,
                 (unsigned long)tif->tif_dir.td_nstrips);
    return ((tmsize_t)(-1));
  }
  return (TIFFAppendToStrip(tif, tile, (uint8_t*)data, cc) ? cc : (tmsize_t)(-1));
}
```

2026-08-28 20:01:58
Response for query 305 after 0.84s:
`TIFFWriteRawTile` writes raw, already-encoded tile data directly to a TIFF tile. Use it only when tile writing is allowed and `tile < td_nstrips`; otherwise it returns `-1`. On success it appends the data and returns `cc`.
