Task: Write a C fuzz driver program to fuzz the library libtiff using the information provided below. Reply with only the content of the C source file enclosed in triple backticks (```), without any additional explanation.

## Target API Functions

1. `TIFFGetReadProc`
​ `TIFFGetReadProc` returns the current read callback stored in a `TIFF*`. Use it to inspect which function libtiff will call for reads. It doesn’t read data itself; it just returns `tif->tif_readproc` (or NULL if unset).
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern TIFFReadWriteProc TIFFGetReadProc(TIFF*);
​ ```
2. `TIFFGetWriteProc`
​ `TIFFGetWriteProc` returns the current write callback stored in a `TIFF*`. Use it to inspect which function libtiff will use for output I/O. It does not write data or modify state; it simply returns `tif->tif_writeproc` (or whatever is currently set).
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern TIFFReadWriteProc TIFFGetWriteProc(TIFF*);
​ ```
3. `TIFFGetUnmapFileProc`
​ `TIFFGetUnmapFileProc` returns the current file-unmap callback stored in a `TIFF*`. Use it to inspect which unmap routine a TIFF handle will use. It does no work itself; it just returns `tif->tif_unmapproc`, or whatever is currently set.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern TIFFUnmapFileProc TIFFGetUnmapFileProc(TIFF*);
​ ```
4. `TIFFClientOpen`
​ `TIFFClientOpen` creates a TIFF handle using caller-supplied I/O callbacks, so libtiff can read/write from custom sources (memory, sockets, etc.). Pass `name/mode`, `clientdata`, and valid read/write/seek/close/size/map/unmap funcs. It returns `TIFF*` or fails if setup/config is invalid.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern TIFF* TIFFClientOpen(const char*, const char*,
 thandle_t,
 TIFFReadWriteProc, TIFFReadWriteProc,
 TIFFSeekProc, TIFFCloseProc,
 TIFFSizeProc,
 TIFFMapFileProc, TIFFUnmapFileProc);
​ ```
5. `TIFFGetCloseProc`
​ `TIFFGetCloseProc` returns the current close callback stored in a `TIFF*`. Use it to inspect which `TIFFCloseProc` will be used when the TIFF is closed. It just returns `tif->tif_closeproc`; no side effects or special cases.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern TIFFCloseProc TIFFGetCloseProc(TIFF*);
​ ```
6. `TIFFSetClientdata`
​ `TIFFSetClientdata` sets `tif->tif_clientdata` to `newvalue` and returns the previous value. Use it to replace the TIFF handle’s client-data pointer/handle. It has no validation or side effects beyond the assignment.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern thandle_t TIFFSetClientdata(TIFF*, thandle_t);
​ ```

