Task: Write a C fuzz driver program to fuzz the library libtiff using the information provided below. Reply with only the content of the C source file enclosed in triple backticks (```), without any additional explanation.

## Target API Functions

1. `TIFFError`
​ `TIFFError` reports a libtiff error message. Call it with a module name and `printf`-style format string. It forwards the message to the installed error handlers; if none are set, it does nothing.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern void TIFFError(const char*, const char*, ...) TIFF_ATTRIBUTE((__format__(__printf__, 2, 3)));
​ ```
2. `TIFFWarningExt`
​ `TIFFWarningExt` emits a libtiff warning, optionally with an I/O handle `fd`. Pass `module` and `printf`-style `fmt` plus args. It calls the installed warning handlers if present; if none are set, it does nothing.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern void TIFFWarningExt(thandle_t, const char*, const char*, ...) TIFF_ATTRIBUTE((__format__(__printf__, 3, 4)));
​ ```
3. `TIFFSetWarningHandlerExt`
​ `TIFFSetWarningHandlerExt` sets libtiff’s extended warning callback and returns the previous one. Pass a `TIFFErrorHandlerExt` to replace the current handler; it’s used for warning reporting, and the old handler is returned so you can restore it later.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern TIFFErrorHandlerExt TIFFSetWarningHandlerExt(TIFFErrorHandlerExt);
​ ```
4. `TIFFErrorExt`
​ `TIFFErrorExt` reports a TIFF error via the registered error handlers. Call it with a file handle, module name, and printf-style format string. If `_TIFFerrorHandler` and/or `_TIFFerrorHandlerExt` are set, both are invoked; if none are set, it does nothing.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern void TIFFErrorExt(thandle_t, const char*, const char*, ...) TIFF_ATTRIBUTE((__format__(__printf__, 3, 4)));
​ ```
5. `TIFFSetErrorHandlerExt`
​ `TIFFSetErrorHandlerExt` sets libtiff’s extended error callback and returns the previous handler. Use it to install your own `TIFFErrorHandlerExt`; pass `NULL` to disable it. If called repeatedly, each call replaces the current handler and yields the old one.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern TIFFErrorHandlerExt TIFFSetErrorHandlerExt(TIFFErrorHandlerExt);
​ ```
6. `TIFFWarning`
​ `TIFFWarning` is libtiff’s warning-reporting API. Call it with a module name and `printf`-style format string; it forwards the message to the installed warning handler(s). If no handler is set, it does nothing. It may invoke both legacy and extended handlers.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern void TIFFWarning(const char*, const char*, ...) TIFF_ATTRIBUTE((__format__(__printf__, 2, 3)));
​ ```

