## Target API Functions

1. `TIFFSwabArrayOfLong8`
​ `TIFFSwabArrayOfLong8` byte-swaps an array of 64-bit integers in place. Use it on `n` `uint64_t` values when TIFF data endianness differs from host order. It always swaps each element; `n<=0` does nothing.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern void TIFFSwabArrayOfLong8(uint64_t* lp, tmsize_t n);
​ ```
2. `TIFFSwabArrayOfDouble`
​ Swaps byte order of each `double` in-place for `n` elements. Use it on arrays when TIFF data endianness differs from host. It assumes `sizeof(double)==8`; `n==0` does nothing.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern void TIFFSwabArrayOfDouble(double* dp, tmsize_t n);
​ ```
3. `TIFFSwabFloat`
​ `TIFFSwabFloat` byte-swaps a 4-byte `float` in place. Use it on a valid `float*` when converting between endianness. It asserts `sizeof(float)==4`; otherwise behavior is not supported.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern void TIFFSwabFloat(float*);
​ ```
4. `TIFFSwabArrayOfFloat`
​ `TIFFSwabArrayOfFloat` byte-swaps an array of 32-bit `float`s in place. Use it when TIFF data endianness differs from host order. It assumes `sizeof(float)==4`; for each of `n` elements, it reverses the 4 bytes.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern void TIFFSwabArrayOfFloat(float* fp, tmsize_t n);
​ ```
5. `TIFFSwabArrayOfLong`
​ `TIFFSwabArrayOfLong` byte-swaps an array of 32-bit unsigned integers in place, converting each value’s endianness. Use it on `lp` with `n` elements before/after I/O when host and file byte order differ. `n==0` does nothing; it assumes `sizeof(uint32_t)==4`.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern void TIFFSwabArrayOfLong(uint32_t* lp, tmsize_t n);
​ ```
6. `TIFFSwabDouble`
​ `TIFFSwabDouble` byte-swaps a `double` in place for endian conversion. Pass a valid `double*`; it reverses the 8 bytes directly. It assumes `sizeof(double)==8` (asserts). Use it only when converting between little- and big-endian data.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern void TIFFSwabDouble(double*);
​ ```

