Task: Write a C fuzz driver program to fuzz the library libtiff using the information provided below. Reply with only the content of the C source file enclosed in triple backticks (```), without any additional explanation.

## Target API Functions

1. `TIFFSwabArrayOfLong8`
​ `TIFFSwabArrayOfLong8` byte-swaps an array of 64-bit integers in place. Use it on `n` `uint64_t` values when TIFF data endianness differs from host order. It always swaps each element; `n<=0` does nothing.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern void TIFFSwabArrayOfLong8(uint64_t* lp, tmsize_t n);
​ ```
2. `TIFFSwabArrayOfDouble`
​ Swaps byte order of each `double` in-place for `n` elements. Use it on arrays when TIFF data endianness differs from host. It assumes `sizeof(double)==8`; `n==0` does nothing.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern void TIFFSwabArrayOfDouble(double* dp, tmsize_t n);
​ ```
3. `TIFFSwabLong8`
​ `TIFFSwabLong8` byte-swaps one 64-bit unsigned integer in place. Use it on a `uint64_t*` when converting between little- and big-endian data. It always swaps all 8 bytes; `assert` enforces `uint64_t` is 8 bytes.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern void TIFFSwabLong8(uint64_t*);
​ ```
4. `TIFFSwabFloat`
​ `TIFFSwabFloat` byte-swaps a 4-byte `float` in place. Use it on a valid `float*` when converting between endianness. It asserts `sizeof(float)==4`; otherwise behavior is not supported.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern void TIFFSwabFloat(float*);
​ ```
5. `TIFFSwabArrayOfShort`
​ `TIFFSwabArrayOfShort` byte-swaps an array of 16-bit values in place, converting each `uint16_t` between little/big-endian. Use it on `wp` with `n` elements. It always swaps every item; `n<=0` does nothing.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern void TIFFSwabArrayOfShort(uint16_t* wp, tmsize_t n);
​ ```
6. `TIFFSwabArrayOfLong`
​ `TIFFSwabArrayOfLong` byte-swaps an array of 32-bit unsigned integers in place, converting each value’s endianness. Use it on `lp` with `n` elements before/after I/O when host and file byte order differ. `n==0` does nothing; it assumes `sizeof(uint32_t)==4`.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern void TIFFSwabArrayOfLong(uint32_t* lp, tmsize_t n);
​ ```

## Related Data Types

```c
/*
 * The following typedefs define the intrinsic size of
 * data types used in the *exported* interfaces. These
 * definitions depend on the proper definition of types
 * in tiff.h. Note also that the varargs interface used
 * to pass tag types and values uses the types defined in
 * tiff.h directly.
 *
 * NB: ttag_t is unsigned int and not unsigned short because
 * ANSI C requires that the type before the ellipsis be a
 * promoted type (i.e. one of int, unsigned int, pointer,
 * or double) and because we defined pseudo-tags that are
 * outside the range of legal Aldus-assigned tags.
 * NB: tsize_t is signed and not unsigned because some functions
 * return -1.
 * NB: toff_t is not off_t for many reasons; TIFFs max out at
 * 32-bit file offsets, and BigTIFF maxes out at 64-bit
 * offsets being the most important, and to ensure use of
 * a consistently unsigned type across architectures.
 * Prior to libtiff 4.0, this was an unsigned 32 bit type.
 */
/*
 * this is the machine addressing size type, only it's signed, so make it
 * int32_t on 32bit machines, int64_t on 64bit machines
 */
typedef TIFF_SSIZE_T tmsize_t;
