Task: Write a C fuzz driver program to fuzz the library libtiff using the information provided below. Reply with only the content of the C source file enclosed in triple backticks (```), without any additional explanation.

## Target API Functions

1. `TIFFSetMode`
​ `TIFFSetMode` simply sets `tif->tif_mode` to the given `mode` and returns the previous mode. Use it on a valid `TIFF*` to change the internal mode flag; it has no other checks or side effects.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern int TIFFSetMode(TIFF*, int);
​ ```
2. `TIFFIsUpSampled`
​ `TIFFIsUpSampled(TIFF*)` is a simple query API that reports whether the TIFF handle is in “upsampled” mode. Use it on a valid `TIFF*` after opening/configuring the file; it returns nonzero if upsampling is enabled, 0 otherwise.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern int TIFFIsUpSampled(TIFF*);
​ ```
3. `TIFFFdOpen`
​ `TIFFFdOpen` creates a `TIFF*` from an existing file descriptor on Win32, using libtiff client I/O callbacks. Use it with a valid `fd`, file `name`, and `mode`. On success it returns a TIFF handle and stores `fd`; on failure it returns `NULL`.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
/* __WIN32__ */
extern TIFF* TIFFFdOpen(int, const char*, const char*);
​ ```
4. `TIFFGetMode`
​ `TIFFGetMode(TIFF*)` is a simple accessor that returns the TIFF handle’s open mode (`tif_mode`). Use it on an already opened `TIFF*` to query how the file was opened; it just returns the stored mode value and does no validation or I/O.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern int TIFFGetMode(TIFF*);
​ ```
5. `TIFFWriteCheck`
​ `TIFFWriteCheck` validates a TIFF before writing. Use it before outputting data: it rejects read-only files, mismatched write mode (tiles vs scanlines), and missing required fields like `ImageWidth`. On failure it reports via `TIFFErrorExt` and returns 0; otherwise it prepares write state and returns success.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern int TIFFWriteCheck(TIFF *, int, const char *);
​ ```
6. `TIFFRewriteDirectory`
​ `TIFFRewriteDirectory` rewrites the current directory entry. If the directory was never written (`tif_diroff==0`), it just calls `TIFFWriteDirectory`. Otherwise it clears the old directory link in the header so the directory can be written again later. Returns 0 on header write error.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern int TIFFRewriteDirectory(TIFF *);
​ ```

## Related Data Types

```c
struct tiff {
 char* tif_name; /* name of open file */
 int tif_fd; /* open file descriptor */
 int tif_mode; /* open mode (O_*) */
 uint32_t tif_flags;
#define TIFF_FILLORDER 0x00003U /* natural bit fill order for machine */
#define TIFF_DIRTYHEADER 0x00004U /* header must be written on close */
#define TIFF_DIRTYDIRECT 0x00008U /* current directory must be written */
#define TIFF_BUFFERSETUP 0x00010U /* data buffers setup */
#define TIFF_CODERSETUP 0x00020U /* encoder/decoder setup done */
#define TIFF_BEENWRITING 0x00040U /* written 1+ scanlines to file */
#define TIFF_SWAB 0x00080U /* byte swap file information */
#define TIFF_NOBITREV 0x00100U /* inhibit bit reversal logic */
#define TIFF_MYBUFFER 0x00200U /* my raw data buffer; free on close */
#define TIFF_ISTILED 0x00400U /* file is tile, not strip- based */
#define TIFF_MAPPED 0x00800U /* file is mapped into memory */
#define TIFF_POSTENCODE 0x01000U /* need call to postencode routine */
#define TIFF_INSUBIFD 0x02000U /* currently writing a subifd */
#define TIFF_UPSAMPLED 0x04000U /* library is doing data up-sampling */
#define TIFF_STRIPCHOP 0x08000U /* enable strip chopping support */
#define TIFF_HEADERONLY 0x10000U /* read header only, do not process the first directory */
#define TIFF_NOREADRAW 0x20000U /* skip reading of raw uncompressed image data */
#define TIFF_INCUSTOMIFD 0x40000U /* currently writing a custom IFD */
#define TIFF_BIGTIFF 0x80000U /* read/write bigtiff */
#define TIFF_BUF4WRITE 0x100000U /* rawcc bytes are for writing */
#define TIFF_DIRTYSTRIP 0x200000U /* stripoffsets/stripbytecount dirty*/
#define TIFF_PERSAMPLE 0x400000U /* get/set per sample tags as arrays */
