Task: Write a C fuzz driver program to fuzz the library libtiff using the information provided below. Reply with only the content of the C source file enclosed in triple backticks (```), without any additional explanation.

## Target API Functions

1. `TIFFSwabLong8`
​ `TIFFSwabLong8` byte-swaps one 64-bit unsigned integer in place. Use it on a `uint64_t*` when converting between little- and big-endian data. It always swaps all 8 bytes; `assert` enforces `uint64_t` is 8 bytes.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern void TIFFSwabLong8(uint64_t*);
​ ```
2. `TIFFSwabArrayOfTriples`
​ Swaps each 3-byte element in-place: bytes 0 and 2 are exchanged, byte 1 stays unchanged. Use it on arrays of “triples” when byte order must be converted. It processes `n` triples; if `n<=0`, it does nothing.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern void TIFFSwabArrayOfTriples(uint8_t* tp, tmsize_t n);
​ ```
3. `TIFFSwabArrayOfFloat`
​ `TIFFSwabArrayOfFloat` byte-swaps an array of 32-bit `float`s in place. Use it when TIFF data endianness differs from host order. It assumes `sizeof(float)==4`; for each of `n` elements, it reverses the 4 bytes.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern void TIFFSwabArrayOfFloat(float* fp, tmsize_t n);
​ ```
4. `TIFFSwabFloat`
​ `TIFFSwabFloat` byte-swaps a 4-byte `float` in place. Use it on a valid `float*` when converting between endianness. It asserts `sizeof(float)==4`; otherwise behavior is not supported.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern void TIFFSwabFloat(float*);
​ ```
5. `TIFFSwabLong`
​ `TIFFSwabLong` byte-swaps a 32-bit `uint32_t` in place. Use it on a valid pointer to one 4-byte value when converting endianness. It simply reverses the 4 bytes; behavior is undefined for null/invalid pointers.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern void TIFFSwabLong(uint32_t*);
​ ```
6. `TIFFSwabShort`
​ `TIFFSwabShort` byte-swaps a 16-bit `uint16_t` in place. Pass a valid pointer to one short; it reverses the two bytes to convert between endiannesses. It assumes `sizeof(uint16_t)==2` and modifies the value directly.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```c
extern void TIFFSwabShort(uint16_t*);
​ ```

